{"title":"Convex function","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A convex function is a continuous function whose value at the midpoint of every interval in its domain does not exceed the arithmetic mean of its values at the ends of the interval.\n</p><p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Function\" title=\"Function\">function</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/4/1846daf63f9c7ff8110fdab2c547e11fe1f6c875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f: I \\mapsto \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" /> for some interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/5/6754299c795eea749abc0763b803bb1b4badf825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> is <i>convex</i> (sometimes written <i>concave up</i>) over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> if and only if the set of all points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e4870695bc9dc560d7e076421b74311d08a6c79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\ge f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Convex_set\" title=\"Convex set\"> convex</a>.  Equivalently, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is convex if for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/5/c45e87e4193d03b8a7f5dc7bf552560b461c2dae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda \\in [0,1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> and every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/731c356680b88d94e638121ba56b9f060bead68a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y \\in I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />,\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/4/8d46c6358e0633248170def7454e968bf6f571f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda f(x) + (1-\\lambda)f(y) \\ge f\\left( \\lambda x + (1-\\lambda) y \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"318\" height=\"18\" />.</center>\n<p>We say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is <b>strictly convex</b> if equality occurs only when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/0110f1bb04c51b2a4d431bf14489fc1b48b37421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b37877eacf63c8c6c739a736be6b5c0c41074d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda \\in \\{ 0,1 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Usually, when we do not specify <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we mean <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/5/5056d8efb16507a1da5385f1bfc64e4b326a57c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I = \\mathbb{R}$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>We say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is (strictly) <b>concave</b> (or, occasionally, that it is <i>concave down</i>) if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/9/0c9607a8b89a6fa56211744bda3ea738c5e76647.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"24\" height=\"16\" /> is (strictly) convex.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is differentiable on an interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then it is convex on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/f/4cfc32b0aa554c9d98af355dafe67283ad403820.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"17\" /> is non-decreasing on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Similarly, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is twice differentiable over an interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we say it is convex over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3ce53bf2e89dfffa10f30fb7ace3f59552f8b151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;&#39;(x) \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcba95962df051ada9f0cacf1da35e7ce20e887d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Note that in our previous paragraph, our requirements that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is differentiable and twice differentiable are crucial.  For a simple example, consider the function\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/3/e83c8cda4016dbc917733aa8993463487f522002.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\lfloor x \\rfloor (x - \\lfloor x \\rfloor ) + {\\lfloor x \\rfloor \\choose 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"232\" height=\"53\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>defined over the non-negative reals.\nIt is piecewise differentiable, but at infinitely many points (for all natural numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, to be exact) it is not differentiable.  Nevertheless, it is convex.  More significantly, consider the function\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/8/2b8700597629b0e140c92a0518aa8a212478c45e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\left( |x| - 1 \\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>over the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/0/2f005f6ee1a0ee8541a7adfeb17a5f855c240230.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-2, 2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />.  It is continuous, and twice differentiable at every point except <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/c/dfc3ae001301c0b3806d9027a9b12b2bd08bec01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${} (0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />.  Furthermore, its second derivative is greater than 0, wherever it is defined.  But its graph is shaped like a curvy W, and it is not convex over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f60010fd01c6801d1b857f1acefb200f1ee8c682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-2,2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />, although it is convex over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55a2deada78acc1831c348210e10b1e6a6ede5a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-2,0]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> and over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/7/9076ffb2b9c051f1b6f07bf18066581d57216258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Convex_function&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Convex_function&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Jensen%27s_Inequality\" title=\"Jensen&#39;s Inequality\">Jensen's Inequality</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Karamata%27s_Inequality\" title=\"Karamata&#39;s Inequality\">Karamata's Inequality</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018081601\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.033 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 188/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 286/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6323/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.241      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.241      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2242:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018081601 and revision id 76482. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}